  "result": "No, that's not right, and it matters for your design.\n\n- **Summary:** a model has no memory between conversations. Each call starts blank. It only \"knows\" its training plus the text you send in that call (the **context**, meaning everything the model is given as input).\n- **Why it's tempting:** inside one chat, it seems to remember. That's because the app resends the whole conversation each turn. The model isn't storing anything.\n- **Sports analogy:** it's like a coach who gets a fresh player every game with no film. Memory is the scouting report you hand over before kickoff. No report, no memory.\n- **For your makerspace assistant:**\n  - Save what matters after a session, like a student's training status, in a database or file.\n  - At the start of the next session, look it up and put it in the context.\n  - Only what you load is \"remembered.\"\n- **Python-flavored sketch:**\n  ```python\n  notes = db.get(student_id)  # saved last week\n  prompt = f\"Student notes: {notes}\\n\\nQuestion: {question}\"\n  ```\n\nThis ties back to your record 0001: the model only knows its training plus the text it's given.\n\nQuick question: if a student told it last week \"I'm certified on the laser cutter,\" what two steps would your code need so the assistant knows that today?",
